    {
      "title": "Bhupender Yadav calls for coordinated action by NCR states on pollution",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/bhupender-yadav-calls-for-coordinated-action-by-ncr-states-on-pollution-126111400707_1.html",
      "description": "Union Environment Minister Bhupender Yadav on Saturday said air pollution does not recognise state boundaries, and called for coordinated implementation of pollution control measures across the national capital region (NCR).\nThe minister stressed the need for real-time monitoring through integrated command and control centres (ICCCs), and direct accountability of field officers for violations.\nYadav on Saturday chaired a meeting to assess measures undertaken in Delhi, Haryana, Uttar Pradesh and Rajasthan for mitigating air pollution in Delhi-NCR.\nDuring the meeting, state governments were directed to nominate secretary-level officials for seven cities in Haryana, four cities in Uttar Pradesh, and four cities in Rajasthan for implementation of pollution control measures through field visits and submission of weekly reports to the Commission for Air Quality Management (CAQM).\nThe CAQM was requested to issue notices to non-performing officers.\nOther directions included expediting the",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-14T13:21:04"
    }
